# Read by every build of this repository: on a laptop, in a pull request and in a publish.
# A comment line has to start with '#' in the first column, and every other line is one argument.
#
# How the HTTP transport of Maven Resolver 1.9 (the one in Maven 3.9) repeats a request which a
# server answers with 429 Too Many Requests or 503 Service Unavailable. Only that request is
# repeated, after a pause, and the build goes on.
#
# Maven Central answers a GitHub runner with 429 and a 'Retry-After' of about half an hour. The
# limit counts the requests of the runner's address, which other users share. A request during
# that half hour makes the block longer, so the resolver waits out the whole pause once and does
# not ask in between. It repeats a request at most twice, and it waits at most 35 minutes before a
# repeat. A server which asks for more ends the build. Without a 'Retry-After', the pause before
# repeat n is n times 15 seconds.
-Daether.connector.http.retryHandler.count=2
-Daether.connector.http.retryHandler.interval=15000
-Daether.connector.http.retryHandler.intervalMax=2100000
-Daether.connector.http.retryHandler.serviceUnavailable=429,503
#
# One upload after the other. The resolver sends five at once by default, and Central answers a
# burst of uploads with 429 sooner than the same uploads one by one. It costs a publish a few
# seconds.
-Daether.connector.basic.parallelPut=false
